<h2>Further Reading</h2>

<ul>
  <li><em>The Life and Letters of Faraday</em> by Bence Jones (1870) &mdash; The standard 19th-century biography, rich with primary sources.</li>
  <li><em>Michael Faraday: Sandemanian and Scientist</em> by Geoffrey Cantor (1991) &mdash; An excellent modern biography that explores the connection between Faraday's faith and his science.</li>
  <li><em>Faraday as a Discoverer</em> by John Tyndall (1868) &mdash; A memoir by Faraday's colleague and successor at the Royal Institution.</li>
  <li><em>Improvement of the Mind</em> by Isaac Watts (1741) &mdash; The self-education manual that shaped Faraday's approach to learning. Still in print and freely available online.</li>
</ul>

